  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 20

Iteration 19 landed the allocator fix and the executed pin, and said ADR 0012
was still `:accepted-defective` because that status was written before the
execution. This file is the paper catching up, and the pin chain that follows
it. It is not a new allocator.

Do not overwrite iteration 19. That file is the discrimination and the
sibling-arm reload.

## Paper

kotoba-mir `b37b19e768490fac2a2fc667e432af90af2ae279` (merge of
`agent/adr-0012-executed` onto `ac14016d`):

- `:adr/status` `:accepted`
- `:defect-closed` records Judah 74/841/0 on amu `30370f07` / native `e8642e0`
  / code `ac14016d`
- `:claims :cfg-liveness` stays false
- `:claims :llvm-beaten` stays false

The code that executed green is still `ac14016d`. This commit does not
change `allocate-without-spills`.

## Pin chain

| repo | SHA | what |
|---|---|---|
| kotoba-mir | `b37b19e768490fac2a2fc667e432af90af2ae279` | ADR 0012 executed on Judah |
| kotoba-native | `69e364edf3154aa8fdf7d87535ca73179b4d2716` | pins mir `b37b19e`; comment no longer says wait to advance amu |
| amu | `ddaffb7d25e2afea96a6b60ff13f6e62bc52f981` | pins native `69e364e`; lock digest refreshed in the same commit |

kotoba-native encodings on judah: 170 tests / 2212 assertions / 0 failures.
That suite still does not run a compiled program.

## Execution

Judah loadavg ~1.99. `java -cp` not `-M:test -m`. After the lock refresh,
before the amu pin moved:

```
native-executor-test + isa-execution-test
74 tests, 841 assertions, 0 failures
```

Same two namespaces as iteration 19. The pin bump is docs-only on mir, so
this is a rematch, not a new ranking.

west-pin-put: mir `56aaa4e5`, native `5f28a2de`, amu `7d2e22cb`.

## What this does not change

- Timed `bench` export stays refused (iteration 4 / 5).
- Leaf vs LLVM stays refused (iteration 14). Do not rematch it here.
- fused-srem / extra MOV / FMA / PGO / kototama optimizer stay refused.
- Iteration 17's sealed +7.41% on the 24-live pair is not re-timed here.
- Straight-line ADR 0006 still storing every live-across value is a later
  Generate.
- `:cfg-liveness` is still false; `back-edge?` still sends actual loops with
  calls to all-vreg.
- Do not treat `kernel_call*` fixtures as a conformance corpus
  (iteration 18).
- Do not overwrite 04-19."}]
